# 1️⃣ Revenue & Margin Trend Analysis (Using Period)

## Business Question  
How has recognized revenue and gross margin trended over time?

All revenue reporting must use the `Period` field (YYMM format), not `InvoiceDate`.

### SQL Query

```sql
SELECT
  Period,
  SUM(Sales) AS total_revenue,
  SUM(Cost) AS total_cost,
  SUM(Sales - Cost) AS gross_profit,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Sales - Cost), SUM(Sales)) AS gross_margin_pct
FROM `chris-delgados-data-portfolio.DistributorCompanyDataset.TotalSales`
GROUP BY Period
ORDER BY Period;

Analysis Prompts

Identify revenue growth patterns across periods.

Calculate Year-over-Year growth.

Identify margin compression or expansion trends.

Determine if revenue growth aligns with profit growth.

2️⃣ Customer Profitability Analysis
Business Question

Which customers drive profitable growth — not just revenue?

SQL Query
SELECT
  ts.CustomerNumber,
  ANY_VALUE(cs.CustomerClassDescription) AS CustomerClassDescription,
  SUM(ts.Sales) AS revenue,
  SUM(ts.Sales - ts.Cost) AS gross_profit,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(ts.Sales - ts.Cost), SUM(ts.Sales)) AS margin_pct
FROM `chris-delgados-data-portfolio.DistributorCompanyDataset.TotalSales` ts
LEFT JOIN `chris-delgados-data-portfolio.DistributorCompanyDataset.CustomerSegmentationData` cs
  ON ts.CustomerClass = cs.CustomerClass
GROUP BY ts.CustomerNumber
ORDER BY revenue DESC;
Analysis Prompts

Identify high-revenue / low-margin accounts.

Identify low-revenue / high-margin growth opportunities.

Segment customers into profitability quadrants.

Determine which accounts drive disproportionate profit contribution.

3️⃣ Revenue Concentration Risk (Pareto Analysis)
Business Question

Is the company overly dependent on a small group of customers?

SQL Query
WITH customer_revenue AS (
  SELECT
    CustomerNumber,
    SUM(Sales) AS revenue
  FROM `chris-delgados-data-portfolio.DistributorCompanyDataset.TotalSales`
  GROUP BY CustomerNumber
)

SELECT
  CustomerNumber,
  revenue,
  SUM(revenue) OVER (ORDER BY revenue DESC)
    / SUM(revenue) OVER() AS cumulative_pct
FROM customer_revenue
ORDER BY revenue DESC;
Analysis Prompts

What percentage of revenue is generated by the top 10% of customers?

Does the revenue distribution follow an 80/20 pattern?

Quantify concentration risk exposure.

4️⃣ Customer Lifecycle & Retention Analysis
Business Question

Which customers appear inactive based on recognized periods?

SQL Query
SELECT
  cd.CustomerNumber,
  MAX(ts.Period) AS last_active_period
FROM `chris-delgados-data-portfolio.DistributorCompanyDataset.CustomerData` cd
LEFT JOIN `chris-delgados-data-portfolio.DistributorCompanyDataset.TotalSales` ts
  ON cd.CustomerNumber = ts.CustomerNumber
GROUP BY cd.CustomerNumber;
Analysis Prompts

Identify customers inactive for 6+ periods.

Estimate revenue lost from churned customers.

Compare churn rates across segmentation classes.

5️⃣ Segmentation Performance Analysis
Business Question

Which customer segments generate the strongest revenue and margin performance?

SQL Query
SELECT
  cs.CustomerClassDescription,
  SUM(ts.Sales) AS revenue,
  SUM(ts.Sales - ts.Cost) AS gross_profit,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(ts.Sales - ts.Cost), SUM(ts.Sales)) AS margin_pct
FROM `chris-delgados-data-portfolio.DistributorCompanyDataset.TotalSales` ts
LEFT JOIN `chris-delgados-data-portfolio.DistributorCompanyDataset.CustomerSegmentationData` cs
  ON ts.CustomerClass = cs.CustomerClass
GROUP BY cs.CustomerClassDescription
ORDER BY revenue DESC;
Analysis Prompts

Which segments produce the highest gross margins?

Which segments drive the largest share of revenue?

Identify underperforming segments with revenue but weak margin.

6️⃣ Sales Representative Performance (Recognized Revenue)
Business Question

How do revenue and margin performance vary by sales representative over time?

SQL Query
SELECT
  SalesPerson,
  Period,
  SUM(Sales) AS revenue,
  SUM(Sales - Cost) AS gross_profit,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Sales - Cost), SUM(Sales)) AS margin_pct
FROM `chris-delgados-data-portfolio.DistributorCompanyDataset.TotalSales`
GROUP BY SalesPerson, Period
ORDER BY SalesPerson, Period;
Analysis Prompts

Compare margin consistency across sales reps.

Identify high-volume but low-margin sales ownership.

Determine which reps drive sustainable profit growth.

7️⃣ Geographic Performance Analysis
Business Question

Which regions show the strongest revenue and profitability?

SQL Query
SELECT
  cd.State,
  SUM(ts.Sales) AS revenue,
  SUM(ts.Sales - ts.Cost) AS gross_profit,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(ts.Sales - ts.Cost), SUM(ts.Sales)) AS margin_pct
FROM `chris-delgados-data-portfolio.DistributorCompanyDataset.TotalSales` ts
LEFT JOIN `chris-delgados-data-portfolio.DistributorCompanyDataset.CustomerData` cd
  ON ts.CustomerNumber = cd.CustomerNumber
GROUP BY cd.State
ORDER BY revenue DESC;
Analysis Prompts

Identify high-margin geographic regions.

Compare revenue dispersion across states.

Determine regional profitability imbalances.
